{"id": "EUVD-2026-103877", "enisaUuid": "bef111f5-b080-3745-8351-de642244121f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: flowtable: generalize pending status bit\n\nRename NF_FLOW_HW_PENDING to NF_FLOW_PENDING and use it to inhibit the\nflowtable GC worker until pending hw offload work has been completed.\n\nApparently, nf_flow_offload_stats() can schedule work to retrieve stats\nwhile the flow is being removed by GC.\n\nAnd this bit can also be used in a follow up patch to disable GC until\nthe flow has been fully added in both directions.\n\nRevert the reordering done in commit d644b23afe1e (\"netfilter:\nflowtable: publish HW_DEAD after worker is done\") to prevent a race\nbetween GC and hw offload handler.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7e292f3c8c853f27a1af7eaf3428a0e76fe5fcc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d52b72f3aa68ad0536444e36530bda75070194c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4033e1a9262c57dfbfc594a591a50fcba63c531a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2cac45848d1cf31ed190db30f90ba8211e9a8ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c549fb7eecd01fdba7c0d12c01da876ef8a3214"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98792", "GHSA-j4c9-hvw2-vg7q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b4b0950-1638-3dac-a459-be99a4bc00d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "1f57613b-67bc-38e4-bd52-169f95a3cff8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "3aeea92d-8294-37dd-8667-d6d9b3349d1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2c8897953f3b2ff5498f3f275708a742bfcdbc24 <7c549fb7eecd01fdba7c0d12c01da876ef8a3214"}, {"id": "46b1919e-acc0-37d6-8f86-fbb7666a2f68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 